{
  "tema": 7440,
  "slug": "costar",
  "titulo": "Costar vs costar a alguien algo",
  "subtitulo": "Cuesta 200 pesos / Me cuesta levantarme temprano.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "Costar = to cost (money): cuesta 200 pesos; add an indirect pronoun to say who paid: nos costó. Me cuesta + infinitive = I find it hard to: me cuesta madrugar. It works like gustar.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Costar** (o → ue: **cuesta**, **cuestan**) has two main uses."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "costar (money)",
              "texto": "_to cost_: **cuesta 200 pesos**. Add **me, te, le...** to say who paid: **nos costó**."
            },
            {
              "forma": "costar a alguien + infinitive",
              "texto": "_to find something hard_: **me cuesta creerlo**."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "For _finding it hard_, it works like **gustar**: the person is the **indirect pronoun** and the hard thing is the **infinitive**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "(a mí) me / te / le...",
            "cuesta",
            "+ infinitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **me cuesta** = it costs me effort. Instead of pesos, you pay in sweat."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dinero",
      "titulo": "Costar: money",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Esos lentes ==cuestan== 400 pesos.",
              "en": "Those glasses cost 400 pesos."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Cuánto ==cuesta== la playera de rayas?",
              "en": "How much is the striped T-shirt?"
            },
            {
              "es": "La casa ==nos costó== solo un millón y medio.",
              "en": "The house only cost us one and a half million."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Cuánto ==te costaron== esos pantalones?",
              "en": "How much did those pants cost you?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dificil",
      "titulo": "Costar: finding it hard",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Me cuesta== creer que se haya ido para siempre.",
              "en": "I find it hard to believe she's gone for good."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Te cuesta== convivir con los demás, ¿verdad?",
              "en": "You find it hard to get along with others, don't you?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Les ha costado== mucho adaptarse a ese pueblo tan chiquito.",
              "en": "They've found it very hard to adapt to that tiny town."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Without a pronoun, it means _people in general_ or _one_ finds it hard:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Cuesta== acostumbrarse a situaciones nuevas.",
              "en": "It's hard to get used to new situations."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Cuesta== creer que estamos en el siglo XXI.",
              "en": "It's hard to believe we're in the 21st century."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "negativo",
      "titulo": "In the negative",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**No me cuesta nada** + infinitive often means _I don't mind, it's no trouble_:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "No nos cuesta nada llevarlos a la central. No está lejos.",
              "en": "We don't mind taking you to the bus station. It's not far."
            },
            {
              "es": "No le cuesta nada llevar los paquetes al correo.",
              "en": "It's no trouble for him to take the packages to the post office."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With **skills**, it can still mean _not finding it hard_:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "A mi maestra no le cuesta pronunciar bien en francés.",
              "en": "My teacher doesn't find it hard to pronounce French well."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
